  "track": "track-07",
  "title": "CSS layout flexbox grid positioning and responsive design",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Layout is the process by which CSS transforms boxes and formatting contexts into positions and sizes within available space.",
    "Normal flow is the default placement model; flex and grid establish different formatting contexts for one-dimensional and two-dimensional relationships.",
    "Positioning and stacking control out-of-flow placement and overlap, while overflow and scroll behavior govern clipping and navigation.",
    "Logical properties map inline and block dimensions to writing modes instead of assuming physical left-to-right axes.",
    "Responsive design combines fluid constraints, viewport and container conditions, and layout changes at meaningful breakpoints."
  ],
